#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Browse, add, and switch ~/.codex providers from a TUI or the command line.

Providers live in config.toml under model_providers. The active provider
occupies the OpenAI slot so Codex keeps using the OpenAI auth flow, and each
provider's credentials are snapshotted as ~/.codex/auth.<name>.json.

Codex only shows a provider's own models when the provider advertises a model
catalog. This tool probes each provider's model endpoint: if it speaks Codex's
catalog format it sets model_catalog_url; if it only returns an OpenAI-style
model list it builds ~/.codex/model-catalog.<name>.json and points the active
provider's model_catalog_json at it.

Everything is read from disk for every action. If config.toml, an auth file, or
a catalog changes while an action is being prepared, the action is retried
against the new contents, so edits by Codex, sync-codex, or by hand are not
overwritten.
"""

